# Registry block folder structure (flat)

All blocks live under `registry/new-york/blocks/<block-id>/` as a **single flat directory**. Do not add nested `components/`, `hooks/`, `lib/`, or `styles/` folders.

## Target layout

```
<block-id>/
  page.tsx                    # preview wrapper (padding)
  <block-id>.tsx              # default export
  <block-id>.css              # block styles (if any)
  *.tsx                       # subcomponents at root
  use-*.ts                    # hooks at root
  config.ts                   # data/constants (was lib/config.ts)
  other-*.ts                  # e.g. code-segments, api.ts
```

## Imports

Use sibling paths only:

```ts
import { useFoo } from "./use-foo"
import Sub from "./sub-component"
import { ITEMS } from "./config"
import "./<block-id>.css"
```

Cross-block composition (heroes embedding integrations/brands):

```ts
import MacOsTerminal from "../mac-os-terminal/mac-os-terminal"
```

List composed blocks in `registryDependencies` in `registry.json`. CSS from a dependency block is allowed when that block is in `registryDependencies`.

Blocks with bundled images or video: see `registry-block-media.mdc`.

## registry.json

- `path`: `registry/new-york/blocks/<id>/<file>`
- `target`: `app/<id>/<file>` (mirror flat layout, not `app/<id>/components/...`)
- Declare every file on disk in the block's `files` array
- After edits: `pnpm registry:build`

## Do not

- Create `components/`, `hooks/`, `lib/`, or `styles/` under a block folder
- Use `../../other-block/` from a file that was only valid inside a nested subfolder (use `../other-block/` from block root)
